### Cleanup user permissions

Asynchronously clean up the specified users' permission data in IAM, including:

- Custom policies and temporary policies
- User group memberships
- Personnel template memberships
- Super manager / system manager / grade manager / subset manager identities

A successful response only means the cleanup tasks have been created; the actual cleanup runs asynchronously in the background. Currently only users (`type=user`) are supported; departments and groups are not supported. At least one user must be provided.

#### Parameters

| Field | Type | Location | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| type | string | body | yes | Subject type. Currently only `user` is supported |
| id | string | body | yes | Username |
| before_at | int | body | no | Cleanup timestamp in seconds. If provided, user groups, personnel templates, and manager identities created after this time are kept; custom policies and temporary policies are always fully cleaned |

The request body is an array of objects.

#### Request

```json
[
  {
    "type": "user",
    "id": "alice",
    "before_at": 1710000000
  },
  {
    "type": "user",
    "id": "bob"
  }
]
```

#### Response

> Status: 200 OK

```json
{
  "code": 0,
  "message": "ok",
  "data": {}
}
```
